(>> Example 4.1: Substation Grounding Grid Design as per IEEE Standard 80) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(Statement: An electrical engineer is designing the grounding grid for a 66/11 kV) Tj
T*
(distribution substation. The site and fault data are:) Tj
T*
(- Symmetrical grid fault current: I_f = 12.0 kA) Tj
T*
(- Fault clearing time: t_s = 0.50 seconds) Tj
T*
(- Soil resistivity: rho = 100.0 Ohm-meters) Tj
T*
(- Surface crushed rock layer thickness: h_s = 0.15 m; Crushed rock resistivity: rho_s =) Tj
T*
(2,500 Ohm-meters) Tj
T*
(- Substation area: A = 60 m x 40 m = 2,400 m^2) Tj
T*
(\(a\) Calculate the derating reflection factor \(K\) and surface layer derating factor) Tj
T*
(\(C_s\).) Tj
T*
(\(b\) Calculate the maximum tolerable Touch Voltage \(E_touch_50\) and Step Voltage) Tj
T*
(\(E_step_50\) for a 50 kg person.) Tj
T*
(\(c\) Determine the minimum conductor cross-sectional area \(sq mm\) of the annealed copper) Tj
T*
(ground conductor to withstand the fault current without melting.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Step-by-Step Solution:) Tj
T*
(1. Reflection Factor and Surface Derating Factor \(C_s\):) Tj
T*
(- Reflection factor: K = \(rho - rho_s\) / \(rho + rho_s\) = \(100 - 2,500\) / \(100 + 2,500\) =) Tj
T*
(-2,400 / 2,600 = -0.9231.) Tj
T*
(- Surface layer factor formula \(IEEE 80\):) Tj
T*
