(1. Arcing Current Calculation \(IEEE 1584 empirical model for V < 1 kV\):) Tj
T*
(- lg\(I_a\) = K_a + 0.0966 * V + 0.000526 * G + 0.5588 * lg\(I_bf\) - 0.00304 * G * lg\(I_bf\)) Tj
T*
(- For 415 V MCC with bus gap G = 32 mm, empirical arcing current is approximately 85% of) Tj
T*
(bolted fault current:) Tj
T*
(I_a = 0.85 * I_bf = 0.85 * 28.0 kA = 23.8 kA.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. Incident Energy Calculation \(E\):) Tj
T*
(- Standard normalized incident energy at working distance D = 455 mm:) Tj
T*
(E = 4.184 * C_f * E_n * \(t / 0.2\) * \( \(610 / D\)^x \) [J/cm^2]) Tj
T*
(- Empirical equation for low-voltage industrial enclosures:) Tj
T*
(E [cal/cm^2] = \(1038.7 * t * I_a^0.957\) / \(D^1.473\)) Tj
T*
(E = \(1038.7 * 0.06 * \(23.8\)^0.957\) / \(455\)^1.473) Tj
T*
(23.8^0.957 = 20.91; 455^1.473 = 8,118.4) Tj
T*
(E = \(62.32 * 20.91\) / 8,118.4 = 1,303.1 / 8,118.4 = 0.1605 J/cm^2 = 3.84 cal/cm^2.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. Arc Flash Boundary Distance \(D_afb at E = 1.2 cal/cm^2\):) Tj
T*
(- D_afb = [ \(1038.7 * t * I_a^0.957\) / 1.20 ]^\(1 / 1.473\)) Tj
T*
(- D_afb = [ \(62.32 * 20.91\) / 1.20 ]^\(0.6789\) = [ 1,303.1 / 1.20 ]^0.6789 =) Tj
T*
(\(1,085.9\)^0.6789 = 116.4 cm = 1.164 meters.) Tj
T*
(- Interpretation: Anyone standing within 1.16 meters of the open MCC during an arc flash) Tj
T*
(will receive second-degree burns unless wearing arc-rated PPE.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4. PPE Selection as per NFPA 70E Table 130.5\(G\):) Tj
T*
(- Incident Energy = 3.84 cal/cm^2 \(Range: 1.2 to 4.0 cal/cm^2\).) Tj
T*
(- Required PPE Level: Category 1 \(minimum rating 4 cal/cm^2\).) Tj
T*
(- Mandated Gear: Arc-rated long-sleeve shirt and pants \(or arc-rated coverall\),) Tj
T*
(arc-rated face shield with balaclava, safety glasses, heavy-duty leather gloves, and) Tj
T*
(EH-rated safety boots.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
