(>> Example 4.3: Engineering Ethics Case Study - Safety Interlock Bypass) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(Statement: During the final commissioning of a 1.2 MW automated industrial stamping) Tj
T*
(press line, the plant production manager notices that the safety light curtains and) Tj
T*
(dual-channel emergency stop \(SIL-3 safety relay\) trip intermittently due to vibration,) Tj
T*
(causing costly downtime.) Tj
T*
(The manager orders the young graduate electrical commissioning engineer to place jumper) Tj
T*
(wires across the safety contacts on the PLC terminal block to allow factory acceptance) Tj
T*
(testing to pass today, promising that a software patch will be written next month.) Tj
T*
(Analyze this scenario according to the IEEE Code of Ethics and formulate the mandatory) Tj
T*
(engineering protocol.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Step-by-Step Ethical & Professional Analysis:) Tj
T*
(1. IEEE Code of Ethics Violations:) Tj
T*
(- Clause 1.1: Engineers must hold paramount the safety, health, and welfare of the) Tj
T*
(public, to strive to comply with ethical design and sustainable development practices,) Tj
T*
