(3. Professional Protocol & Action Plan:) Tj
T*
(- Step 1 \(Refuse Unsafe Directive\): Respectfully and firmly decline to install bypass) Tj
T*
(jumpers, citing OSHA regulations and corporate safety governance.) Tj
T*
(- Step 2 \(Root Cause Technical Investigation\): Instead of a workaround, diagnose the) Tj
T*
(intermittent tripping using an oscilloscope. Tripping is likely caused by mechanical) Tj
T*
(contact bounce or lack of shielded cable on the sensor inputs.) Tj
T*
(- Step 3 \(Technical Remediation\): Install anti-vibration rubber standoffs on sensor) Tj
T*
(brackets, replace unshielded cables with twisted-shielded pairs grounded at one end, and) Tj
T*
(configure the PLC safety relay debounce filter within allowable response time \(e.g., 20) Tj
T*
(ms\).) Tj
T*
