(1. Instantaneous Power Balance Equation:) Tj
T*
(- P_solar\(t\) + P_batt\(t\) + P_grid\(t\) = P_EV1\(t\) + P_EV2\(t\) + P_loss\(t\)) Tj
T*
(- Sign Convention: P_solar >= 0; P_batt > 0 for discharge, < 0 for charging; P_grid > 0) Tj
T*
(for import, < 0 for export.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. Dynamic Load Management \(DLM\) Under Power Constraints:) Tj
T*
(- Total available non-battery power: P_avail = P_solar + P_grid_max = 4.0 kW + 5.0 kW =) Tj
T*
(9.0 kW.) Tj
T*
(- Total demanded EV charging power: P_demand = P_EV1_max + P_EV2_max = 7.4 kW + 7.4 kW =) Tj
T*
(14.8 kW.) Tj
T*
(- Power Deficit: Delta_P = 14.8 - 9.0 = 5.8 kW.) Tj
T*
(- Battery State: If BESS SoC > 30%, BESS injects 5.8 kW to satisfy full-speed charging.) Tj
T*
(- Critical Scenario \(BESS SoC <= 30%\): Battery is protected from deep discharge. DLM) Tj
T*
(controller throttles EV charging current:) Tj
T*
(P_EV_total_allowed = P_avail = 9.0 kW.) Tj
T*
(Equal Sharing Allocation: P_EV1 = P_EV2 = 9.0 / 2 = 4.5 kW per vehicle.) Tj
T*
(Charging current per vehicle: I_charge = 4,500 W / 230 V = 19.56 A \(PWM pilot signal) Tj
T*
(adjusted to 32.6% duty cycle as per IEC 61851-1\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
